Kind: ablation
Issue: #897
Takes out: dup3()'s O_CLOEXEC -- the new name is made without close-on-exec, so it crosses an exec it was asked not to cross: musl_test's [31] must see 22 in the exec'd child
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4
Expect: musl_test: \[31\] WRONG -- .*and 22 crossed

diff --git a/uros/src/lib/libposix-uros/posix_fd.c b/uros/src/lib/libposix-uros/posix_fd.c
index bf883ed8..0e9055dc 100644
--- a/uros/src/lib/libposix-uros/posix_fd.c
+++ b/uros/src/lib/libposix-uros/posix_fd.c
@@ -917,7 +917,7 @@ long __uros_dup3(int oldfd, int newfd, int flags)
         return -EINVAL;
     if (oldfd == newfd)
         return -EINVAL;
-    return dup_onto(oldfd, newfd, flags & LX_O_CLOEXEC);
+    return dup_onto(oldfd, newfd, 0);	/* 897-dup3-no-cloexec: O_CLOEXEC dropped */
 }
 
